<!doctype html>
<html>
	<head>
		<script>
			// function source found here: https://stackoverflow.com/a/40301366
			function addSlashToUrl() {
    //If there is no trailing shash after the path in the url add it
    if (window.location.pathname.endsWith('/') === false) {
        var url = window.location.protocol + '//' + 
                window.location.host + 
                window.location.pathname + '/' + 
                window.location.search;
	window.location = url;	
        //window.history.replaceState(null, document.title, url);
    }
}
		addSlashToUrl()
		</script>
	</head>
	<body onload="javascript:addSlashToUrl()">
		<h1>Page not found (404)</h1>
	<p>Sorry, but the page you were looking for was not found. It may have been moved or deleted, or there may have been an error on this site.</p>
	<h3>Suggestions</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>If you typed in the address, make sure you have spelt it correctly.</li>
		<li>If you clicked a link to get here, the link may be out of date.</li>
		<li>Click 'back' in your browser to try a different page, or return to the <a href="/" rel="home">home page</a></li>
	</ul>
	</body>
</html>
